# Shell scripts must arrive with LF endings in every checkout.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true by default, and so do the GitHub
# Actions Windows runners. Without this line, tools/fetch_external.sh reaches a
# Windows working tree with CRLF endings and dies on its own `set -euo pipefail`,
# because the shell reads the trailing \r as part of the argument.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The DDL and the validators are read as text by Python with encoding="utf-8";
# normalising them keeps a Windows checkout byte-identical to a Unix one, which
# matters for a format project where "byte-identical" is a claim we make.
*.py  text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
